iciencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0684":{"code":"F-0684","title":"Provide appropriate treatment and care according to orders, resident’s preferences and goals.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0695":{"code":"F-0695","title":"Provide safe and appropriate respiratory care for a resident when needed.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0755":{"code":"F-0755","title":"Provide pharmaceutical services to meet the needs of each resident and employ or obtain the services of a licensed pharmacist.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0756":{"code":"F-0756","title":"Ensure a licensed pharmacist perform a monthly drug regimen review, including the medical chart, following irregularity reporting guidelines in developed policies and procedures.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0760":{"code":"F-0760","title":"Ensure that residents are free from significant medication errors.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0761":{"code":"F-0761","title":"Ensure drugs and biologicals used in the facility are labeled in accordance with currently accepted professional principles; and all drugs and biologicals must be stored in locked compartments, separately locked, compartments for controlled drugs.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0842":{"code":"F-0842","title":"Safeguard resident-identifiable information and/or maintain medical records on each resident that are in accordance with accepted professional standards.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","c